WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.730
In 1976, Hong Kong suffered
the Sau Mau Ping disaster.

2
00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:08.710
In 1977, it set up a slope-safety office.

3
00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:14.430
By 2013, it said the risk from its
man-made slopes had fallen by about 75 per

4
00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:14.910
cent.

5
00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:21.630
When Nepal's earthquake struck in 2015,
134 international search-and-rescue teams

6
00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:24.150
came from 34 countries.

7
00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:26.810
So which is worth more:
preventing disasters,

8
00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.390
or responding to them?

9
00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:32.170
In this mission, you'll follow
the disaster management cycle,

10
00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:36.610
and Park's model of how quality
of life falls and recovers.

11
00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:41.590
Then you'll test the tools, from slope drains
and base-isolated buildings to seawalls

12
00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:43.230
and lava barriers.

13
00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:47.850
Your mission: evaluate whether preventing
disasters is worth more than responding

14
00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:48.590
to them.
